@1-5
Imports: homedir finds the user's home directory; serde derives TOML (de)serialization; fs/io/PathBuf handle the config file itself.

@7-23
ConfigError wraps the two things that can go wrong: filesystem access and an invalid TOML file. The From impls let the rest of the module use the ? operator.

@25-51
AppConfig holds the settings saved between runs: the last source file, whether to reopen it, and whether the panes show line numbers. Defaults are all on except the empty last file, and missing fields in an old config fall back to these defaults.

@53-69
get_config loads the config or initializes it on first run. If anything fails, it prints the reason and falls back to defaults so the GUI can still start.

@71-79
save_config writes pretty TOML to ~/.commentor/config.toml, creating the parent directory first.

@81-89
config_path resolves the home directory and returns ~/.commentor/config.toml. Keeping commentor's settings in their own folder avoids colliding with couchy's ~/config.toml.

@91-102
load_or_initialize parses an existing config file; when none exists it writes a default one immediately so the settings file is there from the first launch.
